	'nuances' => array(
		'CONSISTENCY: one English term or label gets ONE Chinese rendering, byte-identical everywhere it appears — desktop nav, mobile nav, menu card, breadcrumb, H1, body, spec table, FAQ, card tag, footer, form option, button, alt/aria text, <title> and meta description. Take the canonical form from the nav or footer and reuse it: if the nav says 轧辍检测, a catalog card must not say 辊轴检测 and a toggle must not say 辊检测. Two synonyms for one on-screen object, even two correct ones, is the clearest proof of two translation passes.',
		'FIDELITY: never add, drop, strengthen or weaken a claim, modifier, number, qualifier or modality. "Addresses manufacturing process deficiencies" is 应对生产工艺缺陷, never 消除; "will confirm shortly" is 将尽快确认, never 几分钟内确认; "Turbocharger flow bench" keeps 涞轮增压器 (涞轮增压器流量试验台, not 流量试验台). Superlatives survive, modals survive as 可／能／有助于, and no 率、度、倍 the English does not state may appear.',
		'Keep a neutral verb neutral and never rhetorically upgrade a flat one. "can significantly impact downtime, machine health and repairs" is 对停机、设备健康状况与维修产生显著影响 — never split it into 减少停机、改善健康、优化维修; "is a promise and our standard" is 既是承诺，也是我们的标准, not the 不仅……更是 escalation. Good copywriting that changes claim strength is still a fidelity error.',
