		'Never change the noun a statistic counts, and give every counter its measure word. Countries stays 国家 (not 市场), people 人才／人员 (not 团队), locations 基地 (not 市场) — buyers put these numbers in comparison spreadsheets. Counter labels are numerals at runtime even though the HTML shows 0, so write 个国家, 名专业人才, 个全球基地, never the bare noun; "home countries" becomes the predicate 个国家设有本土团队. Getting three of four labels in a set right is the classic segment-by-segment signature.',
		'Priority and severity words stay inside their own tier and on their own axis, in plain functional register with no 成语: "non-urgent" is 非紧急, never 低优先级; "critical issue" is 严重故障, never 关键问题; "immediate safety risk" is 紧迫的安全风险, never 直接的安全风险. In an intake form this breaks routing and SLA, not just style.',
		'Keep every modifier and every relation the English states. Trailing purpose phrases survive ("for their consumers" = 为其消费者); an adverbial of duration attaches to the verb the English attaches it to ("Watch how we integrate X ... in a few minutes" is 用几分钟时间，观看我们如何将…集成…, never 观看我们如何在几分钟内将…, which claims the integration takes minutes); and the agent of a "for/from" noun phrase survives ("support requests for Bauer customers and other partners" means requests FROM them: Bauer 客户及其他合作伙伴提交的支持请求, not 对……的支持请求).',
